@startuml
title AISafe - DDD Context Map

skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam nodesep 70
skinparam ranksep 70

rectangle "Route / Flight Operations\n<<core>>\n\nRoute, RouteHistory, Flight\n\nACL: client DTOs\nAircraftInfo, AirportInfo, MaintenanceInfo" as Route

rectangle "Airport Management\n<<supporting>>\n\nAirport, Runway, Facilities,\nAirportStatus, Certification" as Airport

rectangle "Maintenance Management\n<<core>>\n\nMaintenanceTemplate, MaintenanceRecord,\nUsedPart, DoneList\n\nACL: client DTO AircraftInfo" as Maintenance

rectangle "Aircraft Management\n<<core>>\n\nAircraftModel, Aircraft,\nAircraftSpecs, SeatingPack,\nInstalledComponent, AircraftCertification" as Aircraft

rectangle "Identity & Access\n<<generic>>\n\nCollaborator, Role\n\nPublished Language: JWT\n(username, roles)" as Identity

Route -down-> Airport : (1)
Route -down-> Maintenance : (2)
Route -down-> Aircraft : (3)
Maintenance -down-> Aircraft : (4)

Airport -[hidden]right-> Maintenance
Aircraft -[hidden]down-> Identity

Route <.. Identity : JWT
Airport <.. Identity : JWT
Maintenance <.. Identity : JWT
Aircraft <.. Identity : JWT

legend bottom left
  Relationships (arrow from downstream/consumer D to upstream/provider U, all Customer / Supplier over HTTPS/REST):
  (1) Route/Flight Ops -> Airport: airport status and certifications for routes and flights
  (2) Route/Flight Ops -> Maintenance: is the aircraft under ongoing maintenance?
  (3) Route/Flight Ops -> Aircraft: aircraft status, range and capacity; flight hours update
  (4) Maintenance -> Aircraft: aircraft data; availability change (MAINTENANCE / AVAILABLE)
  JWT (dashed): Identity & Access issues the token; every context is Conformist to its format
  and validates it locally.

  Each Bounded Context owns its business rules and its data; there is no shared database.
  Cross-context references use identifiers only (registrationNumber, IATA code, routeId):
  JPA relationships across contexts (Flight->Aircraft, Route->Airport,
  MaintenanceRecord->Aircraft/Collaborator) are replaced by ids + HTTPS/REST calls.
  Downstream contexts translate upstream JSON into their own DTOs (anticorruption layer),
  so no context imports classes from another context. Dependencies are acyclic.
endlegend
@enduml
